# PALPASS — System Architecture & Coding Standards

## 1. Project Identity & Stack
- Name: PALPASS (Palestine Pass) - National Digital Identity & e-Government Platform.
- Core Anchor: Citizen's 9-digit National ID (NID) is the primary civic identifier.
- Framework: Next.js 16.1.6 (App Router with Turbopack), React 19.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4, Framer Motion, shadcn/ui (Radix UI).
- State & Data: Zustand, TanStack Query.
- Backend / Database: Supabase (Postgres with Row Level Security, Auth via GoTrue, Storage, Realtime).
- i18n: next-intl (Arabic RTL as primary with Cairo font, English LTR as secondary).
- Validation: Zod v4.
- Primary Currency: New Israeli Shekel (ILS).

## 2. Strict Project Structure Rules
- ALL application code belongs exclusively under `src/` (`src/app`, `src/components`, `src/lib`, `src/hooks`, `src/i18n`, `src/messages`, `src/data`).
- NEVER create or execute routes from a root `app/` folder.
- NEVER introduce or use Prisma (this project uses Supabase Postgres directly with RLS policies).
- Alias: `@/*` resolves strictly to `./src/*`.
- TypeScript is pinned to `5.9.2`. Do not attempt to upgrade TypeScript to v7.x as it breaks Next.js 16 Turbopack.

## 3. Encoding & File Safety
- All JSON and config files (especially `tsconfig.json`, `jsconfig.json`, `components.json`, `package.json`) MUST be written in pure UTF-8 without BOM (`\uFEFF`).
- Never introduce escaped backticks (`\``) inside template strings in JSX/JS files.

## 4. Backend & Security Patterns
- Server Mutations: Centralized in Server Actions (`src/app/actions.js`). Always maintain `"use server"` where required.
- Data Queries: Centralized in `src/lib/supabase/service.js`.
- Security: Respect Postgres RLS on all 12 tables. Never bypass RLS in client-side calls.
- Concurrency: Financial balance updates (wallet payments, donations, fines) must always enforce optimistic concurrency checks (`.eq("balance", current_balance)`).
- Admin Verification: Ensure authorization reads the authoritative role from `profiles.role` rather than relying solely on `user_metadata`.
- Credentials: Never hardcode SMTP or API keys; always reference `process.env`.
